			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Clarify logger command fallback handling\n\nUpdate the comment block for logger commands (`logger:log`, `logger:warn`, etc.) in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`. The inline acknowledgment explicitly states that these high-frequency calls are now primarily managed by the `IS_HIGH_FREQUENCY` fast-path short-circuit established in recent commits.\n\nThe fallback arms in the `mountain_ipc_invoke` dispatcher are described as a safety net to ensure `Mountain.dev_log` receives output if the high-frequency detection logic changes or fails. This aligns the documentation with the current architectural optimization for the IPC dispatch layer.",
			"SHA": "db5faf8431473f060005b186245adfebef81bd7d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
