			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1568,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove redundant menubar update handler logic\n\nThe inline `menubar:updateMenubar` handler, which implemented a per-100-call logging counter and returned `Null`, is removed. These high-frequency calls are now processed exclusively in the `IsHighFrequencyCommand` fast-path block established previously.\n\nThis cleanup eliminates the dead code fallback in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`, ensuring the IPC dispatch layer relies on the optimized path for menubar updates while maintaining a minimal fallback for command routing integrity.",
			"SHA": "8fd7bc239ad2beac6260602e1d1a12261f11e188"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:05:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1568,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove stub acknowledgments for workspace folder events\n\nThe `workspaces:onDidChangeWorkspaceFolders` and `workspaces:onDidChangeWorkspaceName` commands previously returned a `Null` value as a stub acknowledgment to simulate a Tauri event listener handshake on the IPC binary rail.\n\nThese explicit handlers are removed as the actual workspace change notifications are now broadcast directly via Tauri events without requiring a corresponding `ack` response on the gRPC/Vine protocol rail. This cleanup eliminates dead code paths and streamlines the `mountain_ipc_invoke` dispatch logic in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`.\n\nThe workspace state change propagation remains intact through the existing event emission mechanism, ensuring the Wind UI layer still receives updates without unnecessary binary rail overhead.",
			"SHA": "893b99ac4810581ca194db97cdbef1ff40bd3e08"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T00:48:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1568,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add glob pattern normalization and text edit utilities\n\nIntroduce two new utility modules under `Source/Environment/Utility` to support workspace scanning and document manipulation. `GlobPattern.rs` normalizes VS Code glob patterns from various serialized shapes (bare strings, `RelativePattern` objects, legacy `value` fields) into a unified string and extracts optional base directories for bounded file walks. `TextEdit.rs` provides pure side-effect-free helpers for computing UTF-16 line offsets and converting `(line, character)` positions to byte offsets, adhering to VS Code's `Range`/`Position` semantics. It also includes a self-contained percent-decoder for `file://` URIs.\n\nThese utilities are exported in `mod.rs` to be consumed by the `FindFiles` workspace provider and language service layers. Additionally, the build system is updated in `build.rs` to recognize `TierIPC` as a runtime-only configuration variable, and the logging utility `LandFixTier.rs` is enhanced to emit this runtime tier value alongside the build-baked tiers.",
			"SHA": "00a3ccf53ec931b07171c9e1217f006a6cbd4a86"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T00:46:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1566,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement extension manifest NLS resolution and default config collection\n\nIntroduce two new modules in `Source/ExtensionManagement` to prepare extension manifests for runtime consumption. `NLSResolver.rs` handles the resolution of `%key%` placeholders found in VS Code `package.json` manifests by loading and parsing `package.nls.json` bundles, supporting both string and `{message, comment}` object formats. `DefaultConfigurations.rs` scans all scanned extensions to recursively merge `contributes.configuration.properties` into a single flat JSON object, utilizing dot-notation for nested keys and guarding against circular references.\n\nThese changes ensure that localized UI strings and default user settings are correctly extracted from extension definitions before they are processed by the extension host or applied to the settings engine. Both modules are exported in `mod.rs` to enable integration with the extension scanner and IPC handlers.",
			"SHA": "df0df3f19cd2aa052a86a6ac4745b35845d1164a"
		}
	],
